      "__v": 0,
      "_id": "5b8761d1cd5c4a2361548d4b",
      "author": {
        "_id": "5b874be0cd5c4a2361548a6d",
        "alias": "Olive green Mammal",
        "aliasID": "6606a050d90e505763e31eb9",
        "anonymized": false,
        "avatarURL": null,
        "created": "2018-08-30T01:44:00.222Z",
        "name": "Iwannalookatattachments",
        "serviceAccount": false,
        "urlName": null
      },
      "authorID": null,
      "boardID": "58c62efae9868f3662e9d9a1",
      "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
      "created": "2018-08-30T03:17:37.889Z",
      "deleted": false,
      "fileURLs": [],
      "files": [],
      "imageURLs": [],
      "integrationSourceType": null,
      "internal": false,
      "itemSourceType": null,
      "likeCount": 0,
      "mentionedUserIDs": null,
      "mentionedUsers": [],
      "mergeID": "5b876c9dcd5c4a2361548e45",
      "mergedPostDetails": "So I was in the pug watching some people dance on the stage,  they where very good sadly I stated to lag a lot as the world filled up and more and more people came up to watch the show.\n\nLike a lot of people I don't have the best system just an average one but I got lagged out badly by all the avatars close by.\n\nI temporally turned on block all avatars and the lag went away but so did the dancers avatars.\n\nNow if I was friends with the dancers I would still see there avatars as friends are not effected by block all avatars and would be able to see them dancing but I am not friends with them so there avatars got blocked.\n\nI wondered why when you select a person there is no option on how to deal with there avatar only friends requests/block them etc.\n\nSo my suggestion is for a Avatar button thats on normal and when you click it the button changed to blocked then to whitelist or unblock.  The block option blocks there avatar encase its lagging you out or is offensive.  The whitelist which is what this suggestion is mainly about  lets you still view there avatar when block all avatars is selected like they where a friend without them been one.\n\nThis would be great for anyone entertaining or showing of an avatar where you would like to see just them and hide the other avatars to prevent lag.\n\nI know there are other suggestions for personal block avatars but I have not seen any for whitelisting/allowing avatars outside of been friends with someone.",
      "mergedPostTitle": "Individual Avatar Whitelist/Block Option",
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "5b083c460a1c231b197bc1a2",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "A whitelist would allow a player to be in worlds with all avatars blocked, immune to crashers, particle abusers, and offensive avatars with the option to whitelist and see only who you want to.\n\nAn example would be to look directly at someone when they are using a smaller avatar instead of at the head of the default avatar which would be much higher. Also dancers or performers as stated above.\n\nCurrently to accomplish this, a friend request is required. This can be a hassle for the recipient and potentially the initiator to simply be able to see another player while maintaining a certain level of safety.\n\nMy support for a whitelist comes after a night of using the emergency mode multiple times from raids by abusers.\n\nThis could also be used to quickly cycle through users in a world to see which is abusing particles or shaders for kicking/reporting.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
